Z||000000||firstfiero||01-30-2001||10:53 PM||||     I was complaing about my inspection and when I go to pick up my car today they tell me they fixed my brake calibur and don't need another one!!! dropped my inspection from 250 to 125 bucks. I forgot to add this to the problems. My battery tray was completly rusted out. He made me a new one because it was going to take to long for me to order one. Is this normal? On the good side he didn't see any rust under the trunk or anywhere else under the car. That's another plus!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Now if the bra for my car would come in I could hide that nasty patch on the hood and really be happy!  86se||||reg||10
Z||000001||Shiner||01-31-2001||01:44 AM||||Battery trays rust out all the time.  I think it's because that it sits right there beneath the right side grill, and water just pours onto it.  No big deal though, glad to hear you saved a few bucks!||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||01-31-2001||10:42 AM||||Do battery trays only rust out if you are not using a maintenence free battery?  My car, 87 coupe, has 220,000 miles on it, and the battery tray is perfect, and it has lived in michigan its whole life.  Not that I am complaining or anything, just thought that it was kinda odd.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||01-31-2001||05:44 PM||||Battery trays usually rust out unless you have a fully sealed battery, like an Optima.  Even a maintenance free battery will let out some fumes, etc.  The open vent right above it only makes it worse.  The tray on my GT is pretty much gone, the battery is held in place by the trunk hinge... my 84 is a little better, the battery is actually held down.||||reg||
